  "details": "<p>The library is located in a private house in Assur.</p>\r\n<p><img class=\"image-inline external-image\" height=\"797\" src=\"http://oracc.ub.uni-muenchen.de/atae/images/Plan62_AssurPlan.png\" width=\"583\" /></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "In what seems to be a Neo-Assyrian layer inside a Parthian house in hC10IV, excavators found the remains of a library, consisting of about 20 fragmentary clay tablets. The largest group of texts are incantations, but the library also included a prayer, lexical lists and a list of persons, as well as a literary text detailing the netherworld vision of an Assyrian prince. One of the texts, a memorandum, dates to the reign of Sin-\u0161arru-i\u0161kun (ca. 626\u2013612 BC).",
